# Findings this repository cannot act on, with a date by which it must look
# again. Never a permanent suppression: an entry with no expiry is how a report
# stops being read.
#
# The runtime base (aspnet:10.0-noble-chiseled) has no package manager, so a
# finding in its glibc or OpenSSL waits for Microsoft to rebuild the image. The
# 10.0.13 image (built 2026-10-13) cleared the last ones, and none are listed.

# SixLabors.ImageSharp 3.1.12 (in app/Api.deps.json). Fixed only in 4.1.2+, which needs
# a paid licence key for Release builds, so the app stays on 3.1.x and makes each one
# unreachable instead (see the NuGetAuditSuppress entries in
# src/backend/Directory.Packages.props and docs/security-review.md):
#   CVE-2026-106110 = GHSA-j9gm-c75j-xc9q, TIFF CCITT T4 encoder: the app never encodes
#     TIFF (renditions are JPEG/WebP) and the decoder configuration registers no TIFF.
#   CVE-2026-106113 = GHSA-j3p4-wp97-rph4, HistogramEqualization on float TIFF: the app
#     never equalises histograms, and TIFF is not registered.
#   CVE-2026-106115 = GHSA-jjfr-hcj7-qf5w, TIFF CCITT T6 encoder: as T4.
# When this expires: check whether ImageSharp was replaced or licensed, or whether a
# 3.1.x fix exists; if neither, extend deliberately with today's reasoning.
CVE-2026-106110 exp:2027-01-11
CVE-2026-106113 exp:2027-01-11
CVE-2026-106115 exp:2027-01-11
